spans.s:
śrāmaṇeraka,
(1) with f. ˚ikā (not recorded in Pali) = prec.: m., Divy 〔153.6〕; 〔342.27 ff.〕; 〔345.10〕; 〔382.8〕 (all prose); f. ˚ikā Bhīk 〔11b.4—5〕; assoc. with m. ˚ṇera, as its f., Mvy 〔8720〕; Prāt 〔519.4〕;
(2) m., n. of a nāga: Māy 〔221.24〕; cf. Śramaṇa.

śrāmaṇya (= Pali sāmañña, in both senses),
(1) nt., monkhood: LV 〔88.18〕 (read śrāmaṇyena bhav˚ with v.l. in Foucaux, Notes, 〔113〕); Mv 〔iii.331.5, 9〕; 〔389.3〕; Mvy 〔9128〕; 〔9133〕; Śikṣ 〔198.5〕; KP 〔127.9〕; Bbh 〔85.11〕; 〔182.25〕; Ud 〔xi.4, 5〕; Bhīk 〔3a.1〕;
(2) adj., devoted to monks; regularly with mātṛjña, pitṛjña, and brāhmaṇya; see s.v. māṭṛjña for references.
